.TH SPACEGL_CLIENT 1 "2026-04-19" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl_client \- SpaceGL tactical bridge client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl_client
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ gl | vk ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl_client
is the network client for the SpaceGL multi-user 3D space engine.
It connects to a running
.BR spacegl_server (1)
instance, synchronizes galaxy state via shared memory (SHM), and
launches the appropriate 3D frontend.
.PP
Pass
.B gl
to launch the OpenGL frontend
.RB ( spacegl_3dview )
or
.B vk
to launch the Vulkan frontend
.RB ( spacegl_vulkan ).
.PP
The deck and the server share a deployment master key, read from
.BR SPACEGL_KEY_FILE ,
then
.BR SPACEGL_KEY ,
then
.I ~/.spacegl/key
(created when none exists); the launcher script
.BR spacegl-client (1)
asks for it interactively when
.B SPACEGL_KEY
is not set.
.PP
Every server signs the handshake with its own identity key (wire revision
4). On the first connection to a server the deck prints the server's
fingerprint and pins the key in
.IR ~/.spacegl/known_servers ;
a later connection to the same address with another key is refused
("SERVER IDENTITY CHANGED") before the login. Compare the fingerprint with
the one the server prints at boot, or pin the key in advance with
.BR SPACEGL_SERVER_KEY .
.PP
The whole connection runs inside TLS 1.3 (wire revision 5): the server's
certificate is its identity key, checked against the pin before anything
is sent, and the deck prints "Transport: TLS 1.3 (...)". A server older
than revision 5 does not speak TLS: the connection fails with "No TLS 1.3
session with the server".
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B gl
Start with the OpenGL (GLFW) 3D view.
.TP
.B vk
Start with the Vulkan 3D view.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY_FILE
Path of a file holding the master key (64 hex digits, mode 0600).
Preferred over
.BR SPACEGL_KEY .
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY
The master key as a string (legacy; fallback
.IR ~/.spacegl/key ).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_SERVER_KEY
The server's identity key (64 hex digits, from
.BR "spacegl_server \-\-print\-identity" ):
the deck accepts only a server that signs the handshake with it, and does
not consult or update the known_servers file.
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KNOWN_SERVERS
Path of the known_servers file (default ~/.spacegl/known_servers).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_GPD
Passed on to the Vulkan viewer: unset or 1 selects the GPU-driven render
path (the default, with a CPU-driven fallback), 0 the CPU-driven path
(see
.BR spacegl_vulkan (1)).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_GL_PROFILE
Passed on to the OpenGL viewer: 1 prints its draw-call profile (see
.BR spacegl_3dview (1)).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/spacegl_client
Client executable.
.TP
.I ~/.spacegl/known_servers
The identity key of every server this deck has met, one line per
.IR host : port
(wire revision 4). The first connection to a server pins its key and
prints its fingerprint; a later connection with another key is refused
("SERVER IDENTITY CHANGED"). If the change is legitimate (the server's
data directory was replaced), remove that server's line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_server (1),
.BR spacegl-client (1),
.BR spacegl_3dview (1),
.BR spacegl_vulkan (1)
